id: hot-weather
name: Hot Weather
kind: battlefield
weather: true
profile: elemental-fire
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The heat. Steadfast Checks roll 1(WT) lower, and past Natural it halves your Soak
  Value and burns 10(bT) Life Points a Combat Round.
text: >
  Hot Weather: The extreme heat is enough to make even powerful warriors sweat!

  Connected Profile: Elemental (Fire)

  Natural Weather (Tier 1) Effect(s):
  * Reduce the Dice Score of your Steadfast Checks by 1(WT).

  Unnatural Weather (Tier 2) Effect(s):
  * Halve your Soak Value.

  Cataclysmic Weather (Tier 3) Effect(s):
  * At the start of each Combat Round, reduce your Life Points by 10(bT).

---

# The first Battle Weather, so it is also where the shape of one is settled.
#
# --- Standing in it ------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Gathered by the id on the character rather than by a number, and the Tier the player set
# it at comes with it. "The effects of any Battle Weather only apply if you are in the
# Squares that they influence" - and there are no Squares here, so standing in it is the
# player saying so, the way the Light Level is.
#
# --- The Tiers, and why they are tested in here ------------------------------------------------
#
# "Each Tier gains the effects of the earlier Tiers." So this is not three files or three
# alternatives: it is one Weather doing more the worse it gets, and the tests are `>=`
# rather than `==` for exactly that reason. At Cataclysmic all three blocks below are true.
#
# Tested in the file rather than gated outside it, because the alternative is the registry
# choosing which of the three sets to gather - and the answer is always "all of them up to
# the Tier", which is a thing the file can say for itself in one line.
#
# --- Natural (1) ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Reduce the Dice Score of your Steadfast Checks by 1(WT)."
#
# The Dice Score, which is what the roll comes to - not the target it has to meet. This is
# the first effect in these rules to touch either, and the Check had been rolling a bare
# 1d10 against a bare 6 with `steadfast.target` sitting in the Slot table unread. Both are
# derived now, and this writes to the one the rule names.
#
# 1(WT) is not 1: at Cataclysmic it is 3. Which is the whole of what (WT) is for, and the
# reason the Tiers are numbered rather than only named.
#
# --- Unnatural (2) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Halve your Soak Value."
#
# A multiplication on the finished value, the way Pitch Black halves Awareness - "when an
# effect multiplies or divides a value, that is applied to the final value". Written to
# `soakValue`, which floors at the Tier of Power and then at zero, so a halved Soak never
# goes below what a character provides for themselves.
#
# --- Cataclysmic (3) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "At the start of each Combat Round, reduce your Life Points by 10(bT)."
#
# Reduce Life Points, not Damage: nothing Soaks this and no Damage Reduction touches it,
# which is the same wording Collision Damage and Poisoned use. (bT) rather than (WT) -
# written as the rule writes it, and at Cataclysmic the two would come to different
# numbers anyway.
#
# The Round rather than the turn, so it lands once for everybody standing in it rather
# than once per character per turn.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "Connected Profile: Elemental (Fire)." The Elemental Profiles are the Magic Profiles, and
# there are none in this system yet. The id is carried in the header so that whatever comes
# to read the connection has it waiting, and nothing reads it today.

[passive]
steadfast.dice -= 1(WT);

if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 2) {
  soakValue *= 0.5;
}

[automatic/start-of-round]
if (battlefield.weather.tier >= 3) {
  life.value -= 10(bT);
}
